      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T19:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there any cases where a dma buf has been already created, but does not (yet) have a handle?",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7b9d125_fa4f7601",
        "filename": "include/linux/trusty/trusty.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124693
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T20:15:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that would be the usual case, e.g. system heap. In this case the code path is the same as before this patch.",
      "parentUuid": "94a99205_5c5d68e5",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc6d68b5_6307b303",
        "filename": "include/linux/trusty/trusty.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T20:37:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean cases where the dma_buf code should own the handle.",
      "parentUuid": "c7b9d125_fa4f7601",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7ef7684_3d59ae39",
        "filename": "include/linux/trusty/trusty.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124693
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-28T21:02:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the handle was allocated as part of dma_buf allocation, then dma_buf \"owns\" the handle. Specifically what that means is that dma_buf release() code is responsible for deallocating the handle. \n\nI have an example in aosp/1930990, it\u0027s a mock dma_heap for testing that does FFA_SHARE when allocating the dma_buf and FFA_RECLAIM when releasing the buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "cc6d68b5_6307b303",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e038e556_aa8bc68b",
        "filename": "include/linux/trusty/trusty.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-06T11:17:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That example does not cover the case I\u0027m asking about. If we have a dma_heap where we create a dma_buf but don\u0027t immediately lend it we could be in a situation where trusty_dma_buf_owns_ffa_handle should return true, but we don\u0027t (yet) have an ffs_handle to return (so any attempt to share this fd should fail).",
      "parentUuid": "c7ef7684_3d59ae39",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c57d5d1_0b9b85d3",
        "filename": "include/linux/trusty/trusty.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124693
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-12T20:27:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intention is that trusty_dma_buf_owns_ffa_handle can\u0027t be true unless the dma_buf was lent when dma_heap allocated it. (I\u0027m not sure if I understood you point correctly)\n\ni.e. trusty_dma_buf_owns_ffa_handle \u003d\u003d true IFF (1) dma_buf allocation creates the ffa handle (by lending or sharing) and (2) dma_buf deallocation releases the ffa handle (by reclaiming). And trusty_dma_buf_owns_ffa_handle \u003d\u003d false means that the old code path is used.",
      "parentUuid": "e038e556_aa8bc68b",
      "revId": "5311e705b37ccd2d90bda1b95e7972fe38690169",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
